# Cloudflare Pages _redirects - Rep Today marketing site.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# The four Waitlist Source links (US-WL04) open the landing page. A status of 200 is a
# rewrite: the visitor keeps the link's URL and the page script reads its tag. The target is
# "/", not "/index.html": Pages answers a rewrite to /index.html with a 308 to "/", which
# would drop the tag from the URL (seen in `wrangler pages dev`; re-checked on the preview
# deploy before go-live). Listing the links
# makes the links independent of Pages' implicit fallback for unmatched paths. Other letter
# cases (/TikTok, /YOUTUBE) still reach the page through that fallback, which only holds
# while the site has no top-level 404.html; tools/waitlist/check-site.py fails the build if
# one appears. The tags are the contract file's source_tags (tools/waitlist/contract.json).
/tiktok / 200
/tiktok/ / 200
/youtube / 200
/youtube/ / 200
/reddit / 200
/reddit/ / 200
/network / 200
/network/ / 200
